# Schur's lemma for algebraically closed fields
%%%
tag := "Chapter2/Corollary2.3.10"
number := false
%%%
*Corollary 2.3.10* (Schur's lemma for algebraically closed fields). _Let $`V` be a finite dimensional irreducible representation of an algebra $`A` over an algebraically closed field $`k`, and let $`\phi : V \to V` be an intertwining operator. Then $`\phi = \lambda \cdot \operatorname{Id}` for some $`\lambda \in k` (a scalar operator)._
